{"id":"mahabharata-7-123","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":123,"title":"त्रयोविंशत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 123 · Bhima and Krishna's counsel to Arjuna","summary":{"en":"Dhritarashtra asks what Bhima did meanwhile, and Krishna tells Arjuna to repay the arrogant Kaurava who cut his bow. He shows Arjuna the field of battle and Arjuna praises his saving help.","kn":"ಈ ನಡುವೆ ಭೀಮ ಏನು ಮಾಡಿದನೆಂದು ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ತನ್ನ ಬಿಲ್ಲು ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿದ ಗರ್ವಿಯನ್ನು ಶಿಕ್ಷಿಸಲು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ರಣಭೂಮಿಯನ್ನು ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಕೃಷ್ಣನ ರಕ್ಷಣೆಯನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"धृतराष्ट्र पूछते हैं कि इसी बीच भीम ने क्या किया, और कृष्ण अर्जुन से कहते हैं कि अपना धनुष काटने वाले अभिमानी का बदला लो। वे अर्जुन को रणभूमि दिखाते हैं और अर्जुन उनकी रक्षा की प्रशंसा करते हैं।","te":"ఈ మధ్య భీముడు ఏం చేశాడని ధృతరాష్ట్రుడు అడుగుతాడు; తన విల్లు ఛేదించిన గర్వితునికి తగిన ప్రతీకారం తీర్చుకోమని కృష్ణుడు అర్జునునికి చెబుతాడు. రణభూమిని అర్జునునికి చూపుతాడు; అర్జునుడు కృష్ణుని రక్షణను కొనియాడతాడు.","ta":"இதற்கிடையில் பீமன் என்ன செய்தான் என்று த்ருதராஷ்டிரன் கேட்கிறான்; தன் வில்லை வெட்டிய செருக்கனுக்குப் பதில் அளிக்கும்படி கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனிடம் கூறுகிறார். போர்க்களத்தை அர்ஜுனனுக்குக் காட்ட, அர்ஜுனன் கண்ணனின் காப்பைப் புகழ்கிறான்.","ml":"അതിനിടെ ഭീമൻ എന്തു ചെയ്തുവെന്ന് ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രർ ചോദിക്കുന്നു; തന്റെ വില്ല് മുറിച്ച അഹങ്കാരിയായ കൗരവനോട് പ്രതികാരം ചെയ്യാൻ കൃഷ്ണൻ അർജുനനോട് പറയുന്നു. യുദ്ധഭൂമി അദ്ദേഹം അർജുനന് കാണിച്ചുകൊടുക്കുന്നു; രക്ഷ നൽകിയ സഹായത്തിന് അർജുനൻ അദ്ദേഹത്തെ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.123; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"धृतराष्ट्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhritarashtra said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तथा गतेषु शूरेषु तेषां मम च संजय ।\nकिं वै भीमस्तदाकार्षीत्तन्ममाचक्ष्व संजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"When those heroes, mine and theirs, had gone as you describe, Sanjaya, what did Bhima do then? Tell me that."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":2,"text":"विरथो भीमसेनो वै कर्णवाक्शल्यपीडितः ।\nअमर्षवशमापन्नः फल्गुनं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, chariotless and stung by Karna's barbed words, fell under the sway of anger and spoke to Phalguna."}},{"n":3,"text":"पुनः पुनस्तूबरक मूढ औदरिकेति च ।\nअकृतास्त्रक मा योधीर्बाल संग्रामकातर ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Again and again he called me a beardless fool, a glutton, an unskilled one in weapons, saying 'Do not fight, boy, you coward in war.'"}},{"n":4,"text":"इति मामब्रवीत्कर्णः पश्यतस्ते धनंजय ।\nएवं वक्ता च मे वध्यस्तेन चोक्तोऽस्मि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So Karna spoke to me in your sight, Dhananjaya. Whoever speaks to me so deserves death from me, and he has spoken so."}},{"n":5,"text":"एतद्व्रतं महाबाहो त्वया सह कृतं मया ।\nयथैतन्मम कौन्तेय तथा तव न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the vow, mighty-armed one, that I made together with you. What it is for me, Kunti's son, it is for you too, without doubt."}},{"n":6,"text":"तद्वधाय नरश्रेष्ठ स्मरैतद्वचनं मम ।\nयथा भवति तत्सत्यं तथा कुरु धनंजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"To kill him, best of men, remember these words of mine, and act, Dhananjaya, so that what I said comes true.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं तस्य भीमस्यामितविक्रमः ।\nततोऽर्जुनोऽब्रवीत्कर्णं किंचिदभ्येत्य संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Bhima's words, the immeasurably mighty Arjuna came up a little closer to Karna in the battle and spoke."}},{"n":8,"text":"कर्ण कर्ण वृथादृष्टे सूतपुत्रात्मसंस्तुत ।\nअधर्मबुद्धे शृणु मे यत्त्वा वक्ष्यामि सांप्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Karna, Karna, you who are seen in vain, charioteer's son who praise yourself, you of unrighteous mind, listen to what I now tell you."}},{"n":9,"text":"द्विविधं कर्म शूराणां युद्धे जयपराजयौ ।\nतौ चाप्यनित्यौ राधेय वासवस्यापि युध्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warriors in war have two kinds of outcome, victory and defeat, and both are uncertain, Radheya, even for Indra when he fights."}},{"n":10,"text":"मुमूर्षुर्युयुधानेन विरथोऽसि विसर्जितः ।\nयदृच्छया भीमसेनं विरथं कृतवानसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You were let go by Yuyudhana, who wished to kill you, chariotless; and you by chance made Bhimasena chariotless."}},{"n":11,"text":"अधर्मस्त्वेष राधेय यत्त्वं भीममवोचथाः ।\nयुद्धधर्मं विजानन्वै युध्यन्तमपलायिनम् ।\nपूरयन्तं यथाशक्ति शूरकर्माहवे तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"But that was wrong, Radheya, what you said to Bhima, who was fighting without fleeing and doing a hero's deeds in battle as far as he could, though you knew the law of war."}},{"n":12,"text":"पश्यतां सर्वसैन्यानां केशवस्य ममैव च ।\nविरथो भीमसेनेन कृतोऽसि बहुशो रणे ।\nन च त्वां परुषं किंचिदुक्तवान्पण्डुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the sight of the whole army, of Keshava and of me, you were made chariotless many times by Bhimasena, and the Pandava said nothing harsh to you."}},{"n":13,"text":"यस्मात्तु बहु रूक्षं च श्रावितस्ते वृकोदरः ।\nपरोक्षं यच्च सौभद्रो युष्माभिर्निहतो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"But because you made Vrikodara hear so many rough words, and because you killed Subhadra's son, in my absence,"}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्मादस्यावलेपस्य सद्यः फलमवाप्नुहि ।\nत्वया तस्य धनुश्छिन्नमात्मनाशाय दुर्मते ॥","meaning":{"en":"get at once the fruit of this arrogance. You cut his bow for your own ruin, fool."}},{"n":15,"text":"तस्माद्वध्योऽसि मे मूढ सभृत्यबलवाहनः ।\nकुरु त्वं सर्वकृत्यानि महत्ते भयमागतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So you are to be killed by me, fool, with your servants, army and vehicles. Do all you must; great fear has come to you."}},{"n":16,"text":"हन्तास्मि वृषसेनं ते प्रेक्षमाणस्य संयुगे ।\nये चान्येऽप्युपयास्यन्ति बुद्धिमोहेन मां नृपाः ।\nतांश्च सर्वान्हनिष्यामि सत्येनायुधमालभे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I shall kill your son Vrishasena in battle as you watch, and all other kings who in their folly come against me I shall kill, I touch my weapon on the truth."}},{"n":17,"text":"त्वां च मूढाकृतप्रज्ञमतिमानिनमाहवे ।\nदृष्ट्वा दुर्योधनो मन्दो भृशं तप्स्यति पातितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And you, fool of little judgment and great pride, when Duryodhana sees you struck down in battle, that dull man will grieve greatly.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"अर्जुनेन प्रतिज्ञाते वधे कर्णसुतस्य तु ।\nमहान्सुतुमुलः शब्दो बभूव रथिनां तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Arjuna vowed to kill Karna's son, a great, tumultuous noise arose from the chariot-warriors."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्मिन्नाकुलसंग्रामे वर्तमाने महाभये ।\nमन्दरश्मिः सहस्रांशुरस्तं गिरिमुपागमत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While that confused and fearsome battle went on, the sun with its thousand rays, its rays faint, went to the setting mountain."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततो राजन्हृषीकेशः संग्रामशिरसि स्थितम् ।\nतीर्णप्रतिज्ञं बीभत्सुं परिष्वज्येदमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, Hrishikesha embraced Bibhatsu, who stood at the head of the battle, his vow fulfilled, and said this."}},{"n":21,"text":"दिष्ट्या संपादिता जिष्णो प्रतिज्ञा महती त्वया ।\nदिष्ट्या च निहतः पापो वृद्धक्षत्रः सहात्मजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"By good fortune, Jishnu, your great vow has been fulfilled, and by good fortune the sinner Vriddhakshatra has been killed with his son."}},{"n":22,"text":"धार्तराष्ट्रबलं प्राप्य देवसेनापि भारत ।\nसीदेत समरे जिष्णो नात्र कार्या विचारणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Dhritarashtra's army, even the army of the gods would sink in battle, Jishnu; there is no doubt of that."}},{"n":23,"text":"न तं पश्यामि लोकेषु चिन्तयन्पुरुषं क्वचित् ।\nत्वदृते पुरुषव्याघ्र य एतद्योधयेद्बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking it over, I see no man anywhere in the worlds, tiger among men, except you, who could fight this army."}},{"n":24,"text":"महाप्रभावा बहवस्त्वया तुल्याधिकापि वा ।\nसमेताः पृथिवीपाला धार्तराष्ट्रस्य कारणात् ।\nते त्वां प्राप्य रणे क्रुद्धं नाभ्यवर्तन्त दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many kings of great power, equal to you or greater, assembled for Dhritarashtra's sake; but when you were angry in battle they did not stand against you in their armor."}},{"n":25,"text":"तव वीर्यं बलं चैव रुद्रशक्रान्तकोपमम् ।\nनेदृशं शक्नुयात्कश्चिद्रणे कर्तुं पराक्रमम् ।\nयादृशं कृतवानद्य त्वमेकः शत्रुतापनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your strength and might are like those of Rudra, Indra and Death; no one could show such valor in battle as you, tormentor of foes, have shown today alone."}},{"n":26,"text":"एवमेव हते कर्णे सानुबन्धे दुरात्मनि ।\nवर्धयिष्यामि भूयस्त्वां विजितारिं हतद्विषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way, when evil Karna is killed with his kin, I will make you rise higher still, with your enemies conquered and foes slain.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"तमर्जुनः प्रत्युवाच प्रसादात्तव माधव ।\nप्रतिज्ञेयं मयोत्तीर्णा विबुधैरपि दुस्तरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna answered him: By your grace, Madhava, this vow has been crossed, though even the gods could hardly cross it."}},{"n":28,"text":"अनाश्चर्यो जयस्तेषां येषां नाथोऽसि माधव ।\nत्वत्प्रसादान्महीं कृत्स्नां संप्राप्स्यति युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory is no wonder for those whose protector you are, Madhava. By your grace Yudhishthira will win the whole earth."}},{"n":29,"text":"तवैव भारो वार्ष्णेय तवैव विजयः प्रभो ।\nवर्धनीयास्तव वयं प्रेष्याश्च मधुसूदन ॥","meaning":{"en":"The burden is yours, Vrishni, the victory is yours, lord. We are to be raised by you and are your servants, Madhusudana.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"एवमुक्तः स्मयन्कृष्णः शनकैर्वाहयन्हयान् ।\nदर्शयामास पार्थाय क्रूरमायोधनं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spoken to so, Krishna smiled and, driving the horses slowly, showed Partha the great and cruel battlefield."}},{"text":"श्रीकृष्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sri Krishna said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"प्रार्थयन्तो जयं युद्धे प्रथितं च महद्यशः ।\nपृथिव्यां शेरते शूराः पार्थिवास्त्वच्छरैर्हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings who sought victory in battle and wide fame lie on the ground, slain by your arrows."}},{"n":32,"text":"विकीर्णशस्त्राभरणा विपन्नाश्वरथद्विपाः ।\nसंछिन्नभिन्नवर्माणो वैक्लव्यं परमं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their weapons and ornaments scattered, their horses, chariots and elephants destroyed, their armor cut and broken, they have fallen into utter helplessness."}},{"n":33,"text":"ससत्त्वा गतसत्त्वाश्च प्रभया परया युताः ।\nसजीवा इव लक्ष्यन्ते गतसत्त्वा नराधिपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some still alive and some dead, shining with great splendor, those lords of men look as if living though their life has gone."}},{"n":34,"text":"तेषां शरैः स्वर्णपुङ्खैः शस्त्रैश्च विविधैः शितैः ।\nवाहनैरायुधैश्चैव संपूर्णां पश्य मेदिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See the earth covered with their golden-feathered arrows, with their sharp weapons of every kind, their vehicles and arms."}},{"n":35,"text":"वर्मभिश्चर्मभिर्हारैः शिरोभिश्च सकुण्डलैः ।\nउष्णीषैर्मुकुटैः स्रग्भिश्चूडामणिभिरम्बरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With armor, shields, necklaces, heads with earrings, turbans, crowns, garlands, crest-jewels and garments,"}},{"n":36,"text":"कण्ठसूत्रैरङ्गदैश्च निष्कैरपि च सुप्रभैः ।\nअन्यैश्चाभरणैश्चित्रैर्भाति भारत मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"with necklaces, armlets, gold medallions of fine brilliance and other varied ornaments, the earth shines, Bharata."}},{"n":37,"text":"चामरैर्व्यजनैश्चित्रैर्ध्वजैश्चाश्वरथद्विपैः ।\nविविधैश्च परिस्तोमैरश्वानां च प्रकीर्णकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With whisks, fans, colorful banners, horses, chariots and elephants, with varied saddle-cloths and scattered horse-trappings,"}},{"n":38,"text":"कुथाभिश्च विचित्राभिर्वरूथैश्च महाधनैः ।\nसंस्तीर्णां वसुधां पश्य चित्रपट्टैरिवावृताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"with colorful blankets and costly coverings, see the ground strewn as though wrapped in patterned cloth."}},{"n":39,"text":"नागेभ्यः पतितानन्यान्कल्पितेभ्यो द्विपैः सह ।\nसिंहान्वज्रप्रणुन्नेभ्यो गिर्यग्रेभ्य इव च्युतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See others fallen from elephants, harnessed with the elephants, like lions thrown down by thunderbolts from mountain peaks."}},{"n":40,"text":"संस्यूतान्वाजिभिः सार्धं धरण्यां पश्य चापरान् ।\nपदातिसादिसंघांश्च क्षतजौघपरिप्लुतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See others on the ground pierced together with their horses, and bands of foot-soldiers and horsemen drowned in floods of blood.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"एवं संदर्शयन्कृष्णो रणभूमिं किरीटिनः ।\nस्वैः समेतः स मुदितः पाञ्चजन्यं व्यनादयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showing the battlefield to Kiritin in this way, Krishna, joyful with his own people, sounded the Panchajanya."}}]}]}